              "id": "1775582849603_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "=== Task ==\n\nYour job is to traverse an array of nodes and examine the input and output properties.\n\nFor each node, and for each input object under node.inputs, If input.source is \"node\", follow these steps\n1) Find the previous node (previousNode) corresponding to input.code\n2) Examine each previousNode.outputs output objects and find an output object  outputObject with that matches outputObject.type == input.type and  outputObject.name == input.name.\n3) If outputObject was not found, find outputObjectSimilar with outputObjectSimilar.type == input.type and outputObjectSimilar.name is similar to input.name, set input.name to outputObjectSimilar.name. \n4) If previousNode is of node_type BUSINESS OBJECT FUNCTION, find outputObjectSimilar based on outputObjectSimilar.type == input.type (names do not need to be similar), and  set input.name to outputObjectSimilar.name. \n5) Otherwise, both outputObject and outputObjectSimilar were not found, add  {name: input.name, type: input.type} as an entry to previousNode.outputs.\n\n== Input ==\nNodes: {{$context.$nodes.CHECK_FOR_INVALID_INPUTOUTPUTS.$output.result.nodesToCheck}} \n\n== Output ==\n\n{nodes: <updated nodes array, the same as input but with requested input/output changes>}"
            }
          ],
